1
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,740
Checkmate.

2
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:43,250
Oh! That's the legendary hitman for you!

3
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:45,830
You're just saying that.

4
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:48,130
It's been a while
since you let me take you on,

5
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:50,840
but even as a middle schooler,
you're seriously cracked!

6
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:54,550
Well, this younger body 
definitely isn't as strong.

7
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:58,180
But since I still have
all my experience and knowledge,

8
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,770
maybe I can actually move better
in the field than I used to.

9
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:03,600
Were you actually human in your prime?

10
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:05,350
I mean...

11
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:09,190
Yeah, I did get a fresh reminder that
you've always been freakishly strong.

12
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:10,480
Even back in middle school,

13
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:12,110
but still...

14
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:15,490
Don't go all out without thinking
about the consequences again.

15
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:17,370
Like you did with Tenma!

16
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:21,370
Seriously, I'm pretty sure the kids
from home ec are still suspicious!

17
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:22,950
Yeah, yeah. I get it.

18
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:27,290
And apparently, the report I sent
the boss still wasn't detailed enough.

19
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:30,960
How damn thorough does
that doting father need to be?

20
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:33,670
Listen, okay? If you're gonna keep
living as a middle schooler,

21
00:01:33,670 --> 00:01:36,220
the one rule is never let anyone
find out who you really are.

22
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,390
For the boss's mission...

23
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,100
For your paycheck...

24
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:41,470
And more than anything...

25
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:43,930
For your own sake, Boss.

26
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:47,560
At least, that's how
I see things.

27
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:50,570
Yeah.

28
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,980
You're right.

29
00:03:23,990 --> 00:03:26,620
HOME EC ROOM

30
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,500
Ogami...

31
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:29,040
Noren...

32
00:03:29,370 --> 00:03:30,620
I have a favor to ask.

33
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,130
This weekend...

34
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:34,090
would you two...

35
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:36,380
go on a double date with me?

36
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,840
- Huh?
- Huh?

37
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,590
What?

38
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:43,600
President, don't tell me
you agreed to go out with Tenma!

39
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:46,350
I-I-I-I didn't! I have
no intention of doing that!

40
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,560
But...

41
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:50,520
I love you!

42
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,440
I love you!

43
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,060
Huh?

44
00:03:54,230 --> 00:03:55,480
Chisato!

45
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:00,240
He's been showing up every single day,
and I sort of let it slip...

46
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,200
that maybe I could
at least go on one date.

47
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,910
Wow, you fold way easier than I thought!

48
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:05,990
I mean...

49
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,540
a double date?

50
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:08,370
Why?

51
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:13,420
I said, it couldn't be just the two of us,
but if Noren and Oga come, then okay.

52
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:15,170
No, do not drag us into this!

53
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:16,790
You're usually so on top of things,

54
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:19,260
but when it comes to this stuff,
you're hopeless.

55
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:21,260
Yeah, I'm ashamed to admit it.

56
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,260
Get it together! Keep this up...

57
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,640
and someday when you're
one of those businesswomen...

58
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:30,480
who scares off every guy around her
because she's too competent at work...

59
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,680
Chisato!

60
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,650
...you'll get suckered
by some random pushy loser!

61
00:04:33,650 --> 00:04:37,070
I just thought maybe if I went on
one date with him, he'd be satisfied.

62
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:38,230
What kind of a plan is that?

63
00:04:38,230 --> 00:04:42,490
It's even more delusional than
Japan's low birthrate countermeasures!

64
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:48,280
DOKI-DOKI DOUBLE DATE
SATURDAY, MAY 23rd

65
00:04:49,370 --> 00:04:50,950
Somehow...

66
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:53,580
I ended up getting roped
into this double date.

67
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,090
But honestly, I'm still curious
about Ogami's secret.

68
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,960
Maybe I'll find out something today.

69
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,550
Yo!

70
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:03,840
President!

71
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:06,300
Man, I'm really sorry about all this.

72
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:08,180
Wait, what is that outfit?

73
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:12,680
Well, with the duel thing, this is
sort of anti-pickup-guy protection.

74
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,480
Ah, you're already here!

75
00:05:14,770 --> 00:05:15,940
Sorry to keep you waiting!

76
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,190
- That's workout gear!
- Huh?

77
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:21,190
I wasn't expecting you
to show up stylish or anything...

78
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:23,110
but come on! That's workout gear!

79
00:05:23,110 --> 00:05:24,240
Huh? Is it bad?

80
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,950
You know this is a date, right?
Not the gym?

81
00:05:27,490 --> 00:05:32,080
Who the hell said that
Unicorns were perfect inside and out?

82
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:34,620
His stats are ridiculously lopsided.

83
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:37,420
In fact, everything got dumped
into physical.

84
00:05:37,710 --> 00:05:40,000
A date with my beloved Chisato!

85
00:05:40,290 --> 00:05:41,920
I'm so, so happy!

86
00:05:43,170 --> 00:05:44,590
But he's so pure!

87
00:05:44,590 --> 00:05:47,220
At this rate,
he's just gonna steamroll you!

88
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:49,050
Huh? Am I last?

89
00:05:49,470 --> 00:05:51,390
Sorry. Kept you waiting.

90
00:05:53,310 --> 00:05:54,230
A jacket...

91
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:56,100
and a clutch bag?

92
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:56,940
Huh?

93
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,400
This isn't about
whether it's stylish or not!

94
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,270
You're on some completely
different wavelength!

95
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:02,530
I'm pretty sure I got the size right.

96
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,990
That's not the issue!

97
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,490
A date?

98
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,240
Are you sure about this?

99
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:10,580
You're an old man, remember?

100
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:12,370
What choice do I have?

101
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:15,660
If we're just walking around town,
I'll manage somehow.

102
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:19,080
I won't be around
at your departure time, though.

103
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,290
What are you gonna wear?

104
00:06:20,290 --> 00:06:21,960
It'll be fine.

105
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:24,510
I'll just wear something normal.

106
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,760
Your "normal" is an automatic fail, boss!

107
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:30,430
Still...

108
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:32,720
what a weird group.

109
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:37,100
And Noren's outfit is like some celebrity
trying not to be recognized.

110
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:40,440
Am I the only normal middle schooler here?

111
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:46,820
Uh...

112
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:49,320
So, what are we going to do?

113
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:53,950
I figured we'd browse some shops
around here, then maybe catch a movie.

114
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:55,620
That's surprisingly normal!

115
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,750
Thank goodness it's not training.

116
00:06:58,410 --> 00:07:01,750
Man, this used to be just
some nothing park back in the day.

117
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,000
There were even homeless guys
hanging around.

118
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,590
Huh? Back in the day?

119
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:11,430
I mean, I just happened to see
some random old guy write that online!

120
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:13,260
Don't let your guard down, Boss!

121
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:15,930
Old guy?

122
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:18,600
HACHIROU RAMEN

123
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,270
Oh! I've been kind of curious...

124
00:07:20,650 --> 00:07:22,310
about that ramen place!

125
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:25,070
Huh? You like ramen?

126
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,730
What? No...

127
00:07:26,730 --> 00:07:29,360
I mean... I have it
once in a while, I guess!

128
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:33,320
That place has a line
full of seriously hardcore customers.

129
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:34,830
You wanna go heavy, huh?

130
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,910
Sorry, ramen's out for me.

131
00:07:36,910 --> 00:07:38,790
Today's not a cheat day.

132
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:40,790
You're seriously training at that level?

133
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:45,800
Well, I guess
I am getting a little hungry.

134
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:48,380
Wanna duck into that coffee house
over there?

135
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,590
"Coffee house"?

136
00:07:49,590 --> 00:07:52,220
I mean, it's not like nobody says that...

137
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:55,300
but when Ogami says it,
it fits way too well!

138
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,490
Man...

139
00:08:12,820 --> 00:08:15,070
this has been fun, Chisato!

140
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:16,780
O-Oh, y-yeah?

141
00:08:16,780 --> 00:08:19,910
Crap. Somehow I actually had
a pretty good time.

142
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:26,250
I knew it!

143
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:29,840
I thought so before, too,
but it's not so much that he's weird!

144
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,420
It's like he's a totally different age!

145
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:33,630
But plain and simple,
he's a middle schooler for sure!

146
00:08:33,630 --> 00:08:35,640
It's not like he just looks young!

147
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:39,100
Oh, shit!

148
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,940
What the hell? My body suddenly feels...

149
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:04,670
Crap! Did I pass out?

150
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:07,590
Judging by the scene,
has it been about an hour?

151
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,840
Huh? My hands look old.

152
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:13,220
Wait...

153
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:15,300
This stubble...

154
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:18,550
What? I'm back to being an adult?

155
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:20,600
Was there some trigger?

156
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:23,560
Or did the wasp venom
just wear off naturally?

157
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,480
No, that doesn't matter right now!

158
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,150
This is really bad!

159
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:29,020
By "bad," I mean...

160
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:32,530
the visuals! Why now?

161
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:35,570
Could the timing possibly be
any worse?

162
00:09:35,570 --> 00:09:36,280
MIDDLE SCHOOL / MIDDLE SCHOOL
MIDDLE AGE / MIDDLE SCHOOL

163
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:38,620
If they notice me like this...

164
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:41,040
EEK
AAAH

165
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:43,540
Oh, no. I already want to die.

166
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,920
Ogami, is something wrong?

167
00:09:47,790 --> 00:09:48,830
Bathroom!

168
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:49,750
Huh?

169
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:58,510
Now that I'm thinking clearly,
what the hell am I doing?

170
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:02,390
Even if I felt more like a chaperone
tagging along...

171
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:05,520
What grown-ass man goes on a
 double date with middle schoolers?

172
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:06,600
Am I an idiot?

173
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:09,560
That snapped me right back to my senses.

174
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:12,320
I panicked a little,
but I'm back to normal now.

175
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,190
This little game ends here.

176
00:10:14,190 --> 00:10:15,860
I'm just gonna bail.

177
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:20,370
I do feel a little bad about
 breaking my promise to Noren...

178
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:24,450
but an old guy going to middle school
in the first place is insane.

179
00:10:24,450 --> 00:10:25,960
Hey, Ogami!

180
00:10:26,290 --> 00:10:28,210
- Huh? Tenma?
- What, did you fall in?

181
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:29,670
The movie's over—

182
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:31,960
That scared me.

183
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:32,800
Hey!

184
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:35,420
Coming all the way over to the stall?
Of course he would!

185
00:10:36,170 --> 00:10:38,680
Dammit, what do I do?

186
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,430
Oh, we're connected.

187
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:45,020
What happened?

188
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,190
Don't say anything! Just look at this!

189
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:50,230
Y-You're back!

190
00:10:50,230 --> 00:10:52,690
And Noren and the others are outside...

191
00:10:52,690 --> 00:10:54,360
so I can't get out of this damn restroom.

192
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:58,530
All you brought today
was that clutch bag, right?

193
00:10:58,530 --> 00:11:02,280
Lock picks, mini bombs
and a bunch of useless...

194
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:02,910
Oh!

195
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:06,040
The cat-shaped voice-changer sticker!

196
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,250
At least it's not a bow tie.

197
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:10,540
Hey, are you really okay in there?

198
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,040
Stick it around your Adam's apple.

199
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:16,840
Then use the app on your phone
to change the frequency, and...

200
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:18,630
U-Uh...

201
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:21,760
I-I might not be okay.

202
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,430
Huh? Seriously?

203
00:11:23,890 --> 00:11:26,600
M-My stomach's messed up.
I can't come out.

204
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,430
You three go home without me.

205
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:31,310
It's that bad? Should I call an ambulance?

206
00:11:31,310 --> 00:11:35,270
No! It's not that bad!
But I can't come out right away!

207
00:11:35,270 --> 00:11:38,240
We were only heading home anyway,
so just go! Please!

208
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:40,990
Okay.

209
00:11:40,990 --> 00:11:42,530
I'll tell them.

210
00:11:42,530 --> 00:11:44,120
Oh, thank goodness!

211
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:47,580
Now if I just wait a little and come out,
I can get home safe, and—

212
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:48,950
Huh? Wh-Who are...

213
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:50,790
Wh-What the...

214
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:52,250
- Hey! Wait! T-Tenma!
- Huh?

215
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:54,250
- Ogami! Noren just...
- Safety...

216
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:56,000
...is officially off the table?

217
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,460
Noren got kidnapped!

218
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,380
Another kidnapping?

219
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,010
Again with this crap?

220
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:05,260
Noren, even this old man's starting
to feel sorry for you!

221
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,260
Dammit! No, I can't!

222
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,810
I can't just leave her!

223
00:12:08,810 --> 00:12:11,060
If I go home now,
I'll never sleep right again!

224
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:12,230
Dammit!

225
00:12:12,850 --> 00:12:13,980
You okay?

226
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:15,230
I'm fine...

227
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:16,610
but Noren...

228
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:19,940
Boss! If you come out like that,
they're gonna get a good look at you!

229
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:20,610
Tenma!

230
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:22,910
Hug her as hard as you can! Right now!

231
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,030
Huh?

232
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:24,990
Huh?

233
00:12:26,830 --> 00:12:27,660
Like this?

234
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,040
Big Sis!

235
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,290
What did the kidnappers look like?

236
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:35,040
Uh, th-there were two of them!

237
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,130
Both wearing black hoodies!

238
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,380
A black van! Heading toward Gaien?

239
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,350
TENGOKU
GAIENZAKA

240
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:49,220
Huh?

241
00:12:49,220 --> 00:12:50,060
Hey, wait!

242
00:12:50,430 --> 00:12:52,140
Message this number!

243
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:54,770
You'll be reimbursed!

244
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,230
What?

245
00:12:57,730 --> 00:13:00,480
Dammit! One thing after another!

246
00:13:05,950 --> 00:13:08,330
Boss, I just realized something.

247
00:13:08,330 --> 00:13:09,240
Yeah?

248
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:10,950
That whole restroom thing...

249
00:13:10,950 --> 00:13:13,960
Couldn't you have just walked out
pretending to be a total stranger?

250
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,620
Oh! Yeah!

251
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:17,540
I panicked and didn't think of it!

252
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:21,050
Well, that's rare.

253
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:23,760
He's been in plenty of situations...

254
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,890
that called for way tougher split-second calls.

255
00:13:25,890 --> 00:13:29,430
And panicking over anything 
at all is out of character for him.

256
00:13:29,430 --> 00:13:32,310
Was he really enjoying
middle school life that much?

257
00:13:34,350 --> 00:13:36,940
Jeez! How long are you
 gonna keep hugging me?

258
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:38,900
Oh. I was so happy, I forgot.

259
00:13:39,230 --> 00:13:41,150
This is not the time!

260
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:45,650
Ogami went after them alone,
and I don't know what we can even do...

261
00:13:45,650 --> 00:13:47,200
but we have to go after him!

262
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:47,820
Huh?

263
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,120
Why?

264
00:13:50,990 --> 00:13:54,330
As long as you're safe, I'm good, Chisato.

265
00:13:54,330 --> 00:13:55,660
Do I have to go?

266
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,790
Ogami already went, didn't he?

267
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,260
Well...

268
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:06,340
Of course you do!

269
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:08,300
What are you, a robot?

270
00:14:08,300 --> 00:14:11,010
Did you already forget
what we talked about?

271
00:14:11,010 --> 00:14:12,890
When someone's in trouble,
you go to help!

272
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:17,730
Sure, we're middle schoolers!
I know encouraging us to go is crazy!

273
00:14:18,270 --> 00:14:20,520
But that attitude is not okay!

274
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,730
And here I was,
actually having a little fun today!

275
00:14:23,730 --> 00:14:25,570
Don't make me lose respect for you!

276
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:28,280
Someone who talks like that
at a time like this...

277
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:30,410
is someone I could never like!

278
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:35,870
I'm sorry.

279
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:38,620
People have always told me
I can't read the room...

280
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:41,460
or that I don't understand
how other people feel.

281
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:45,130
Even when I think I get it,
I don't really get it.

282
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:48,260
And I'm sure that's
 going to keep happening.

283
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:49,260
So...

284
00:14:50,260 --> 00:14:51,680
I want you to teach me.

285
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:53,470
I'll try.

286
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,810
So I don't make you cry, Chisato.

287
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,100
Okay!

288
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:59,190
I'm going.

289
00:14:59,810 --> 00:15:02,360
Chisato, stay here and call the police.

290
00:15:02,650 --> 00:15:04,150
No, I'm going, too—

291
00:15:04,150 --> 00:15:07,280
You're slow, and you'd probably
just get in the way.

292
00:15:07,570 --> 00:15:09,450
- Hello? Ogami? Where are you?
- You just said...

293
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:11,910
...you were going to try
not to make me cry!

294
00:15:15,950 --> 00:15:17,410
Jeez, Tenma...

295
00:15:17,410 --> 00:15:18,960
He's coming, too?

296
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:21,170
And what the hell is this crap?

297
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:25,670
Can't believe I turned back into a kid
again in the middle of chasing them.

298
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:27,130
Okay, I'm here!

299
00:15:27,670 --> 00:15:28,920
Sorry to keep you waiting!

300
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:31,220
That was fast! How'd you get here?

301
00:15:31,220 --> 00:15:33,140
Huh? I ran.

302
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,930
It was only two or three kilometers.

303
00:15:34,930 --> 00:15:38,230
He's not a triple threat superman
for nothing.

304
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:44,690
There they are.

305
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,690
Those guys...

306
00:15:48,070 --> 00:15:51,200
They don't seem
like your average NPCs, do they?

307
00:15:51,490 --> 00:15:53,280
Are they high or something?

308
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,330
Yeah.

309
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:56,410
Crap! I screwed up!

310
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:59,830
I figured they were just low-level thugs,
so I brought Tenma along...

311
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,460
but that mark...

312
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,330
Their organization's bigger than ours.

313
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:08,630
In number of assassins, track record,
sales, and customer satisfaction...

314
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:11,340
They're number one across the board!
The biggest name in the business!

315
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:13,090
JARDIN!

316
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:16,720
They rank their clients 
based on their membership fee.

317
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:20,140
The higher the rank,
the tougher the assassins they send.

318
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:25,400
Supposedly, only VIPs are allowed
to join the top-tier black rank!

319
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:28,030
Huh? There's two of 'em.

320
00:16:29,230 --> 00:16:30,570
The little one is...

321
00:16:30,570 --> 00:16:32,070
Well, whatever.

322
00:16:32,070 --> 00:16:34,200
Kazuma Rindou, age 15!

323
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,660
Either way, this'll be over in no time.

324
00:16:37,030 --> 00:16:40,790
The big one is Eiji Rindou, age 13!

325
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:45,500
They're both black-rank assassins!

326
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,840
Hold up! They're middle schoolers?

327
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:49,960
Huh?

328
00:16:52,170 --> 00:16:53,510
Hello?

329
00:16:53,510 --> 00:16:54,510
Ah...

330
00:16:54,510 --> 00:16:56,430
Nice to meet you, Ogami.

331
00:16:56,430 --> 00:16:58,810
And Tenma Tendo, as well.

332
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,640
What do you want?

333
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:05,810
Why, the Mitsuoka duel, of course.
And the position of fiancé.

334
00:17:06,270 --> 00:17:07,230
Though...

335
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:09,690
I'll formally challenge you
for that another day.

336
00:17:09,690 --> 00:17:11,280
Today, my goal is...

337
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,780
Noren's heart.

338
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:16,450
My specialty is hypnosis.

339
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:19,700
I'm going to use it
to make her fall in love with Eiji here.

340
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,700
Huh? You can't just—

341
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:23,160
I can.

342
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:28,420
I can hypnotize anyone
powerfully and instantly.

343
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:31,590
If I win the duel,
I can take the position of fiancé.

344
00:17:31,590 --> 00:17:33,970
But merely having the title
would not satisfy me.

345
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,840
Noren Mitsuoka must become...

346
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:39,720
my little brother Eiji's bride
in body and soul.

347
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,390
- Wha...
- Wha...

348
00:17:42,810 --> 00:17:45,020
Um, your brother there...

349
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:48,270
He's only been going
"ooh" and "aah" this whole time.

350
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:51,610
Indeed. My brother is a man of few words.

351
00:17:51,610 --> 00:17:53,860
But once she falls in love with him,
that will be a minor detail.

352
00:17:53,990 --> 00:17:56,740
No, this isn't about a "few words."

353
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:58,240
It's more like, is he alive?

354
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:00,530
Even if, for argument's sake,
they did get married...

355
00:18:00,530 --> 00:18:04,250
could he actually make
a marriage work long term?

356
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:07,670
He moves, therefore he lives.

357
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:11,380
I won't deny there may be certain areas
where he falls short, but not to worry.

358
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:14,510
I will support him. And with that,
our conversation is over.

359
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:15,800
Agreed?

360
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:17,430
Like hell I do!

361
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:18,720
What a nuisance.

362
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:22,180
By the way, Tenma...

363
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:23,020
- Huh?
- Huh?

364
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:23,720
Me?

365
00:18:24,310 --> 00:18:26,440
I have a proposal.

366
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:29,560
You only came here because
Chisato Shiraishi told you to, right?

367
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:31,900
If you leave Ogami behind
and go home right now,

368
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:35,110
I'll use hypnosis to make
Chisato Shiraishi fall in love with you.

369
00:18:35,110 --> 00:18:39,200
You'll get what you want, and avoid
putting yourself in unnecessary danger.

370
00:18:39,870 --> 00:18:41,120
Well?

371
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,370
This guy...

372
00:18:42,370 --> 00:18:44,330
He's done a serious amount of research!

373
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:46,540
Tenma doesn't really understand emotions.

374
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:48,580
Don't tell me...

375
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:54,710
Jeez...

376
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:57,470
You probably shouldn't have said that.

377
00:18:57,470 --> 00:19:00,390
That's basically
like fixing a match, right?

378
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:03,430
The way I feel about Chisato...

379
00:19:03,430 --> 00:19:06,520
is no different from the three sports
I've devoted my life to.

380
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:09,560
If I have to win by cheating,
I'd rather lose for real and cry about it.

381
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:11,810
Tenma...

382
00:19:11,810 --> 00:19:14,190
I mean, I'm definitely gonna win, though!

383
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:17,400
Big Sis, you've got
one hell of an admirer.

384
00:19:17,650 --> 00:19:18,780
So, honestly...

385
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:22,570
I was already getting pissed off
from the whole Noren thing at the start.

386
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:24,660
I don't like you guys.

387
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:27,750
And I'm not really in the mood
to just let this slide.

388
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:31,040
So, there you have it. We're done talking.

389
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:34,250
Give Noren back,
you trash-tier matchmaking brothers.

390
00:19:34,670 --> 00:19:37,210
Negotiations have broken down, then.

391
00:19:37,210 --> 00:19:38,260
Very well.

392
00:19:39,630 --> 00:19:40,630
War it is!

393
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:42,140
Golf?

394
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:48,350
- Crap! Dodge, Tenma!
- Huh? Ah...

395
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,150
These guys are nuts!

396
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:01,950
Ogami! Even I can tell
what's going on here!

397
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:04,120
If that hits us, we're dead!

398
00:20:04,490 --> 00:20:06,290
Yeah, I'm with you on that one!

399
00:20:06,870 --> 00:20:09,790
For now, get out into the concourse
and find cover!

400
00:20:12,710 --> 00:20:14,880
All right. I'll pursue them.

401
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:20,090
You keep watch over Noren, and
if you sense them anywhere, snipe them!

402
00:20:21,840 --> 00:20:24,050
Dammit, who the hell are these guys?

403
00:20:25,890 --> 00:20:27,180
This is bad!

404
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:29,350
Empty-handed, even I might be in trouble!

405
00:20:29,350 --> 00:20:30,020
Boss!

406
00:20:30,350 --> 00:20:32,770
Can you get toward block 320?

407
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:34,940
I sent a drone loaded with guns your way!

408
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:36,150
For real? You're a lifesaver!

409
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:40,860
What's gotten into you, Nekota?
You're absolutely killing it today!

410
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,780
Okay, here it comes! That's it!

411
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,330
I'm not letting you
get your hands on a weapon.

412
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:54,330
You're in the same
line of work, aren't you?

413
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:01,470
It fell inside the concourse.

414
00:21:01,470 --> 00:21:02,880
But it's too far away.

415
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:05,840
And if he can hit a drone
from that position...

416
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:07,680
I won't have time to go grab it!

417
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:11,140
So, it ends before I even use
my real weapon.

418
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:12,560
How anticlimactic!

419
00:21:13,390 --> 00:21:15,020
Boss!

420
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:18,360
The big guy left on the ground...

421
00:21:18,650 --> 00:21:20,190
is the sniper, right?

422
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,070
Wha...

423
00:21:38,670 --> 00:21:40,800
He used the sound to make Eiji snipe it...

424
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:43,300
so the blast wave
would launch the gun toward him.

425
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:44,260
Listen.

426
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:49,260
I basically see Noren as a daughter.

427
00:21:49,890 --> 00:21:51,470
Now imagine you're the dad...

428
00:21:51,470 --> 00:21:54,770
and some guy shows up at your house
asking to have your daughter!

429
00:21:54,770 --> 00:21:56,310
We're in love!

430
00:21:56,310 --> 00:22:00,190
Because I hypnotized her.

431
00:22:05,860 --> 00:22:08,870
Naturally, I'm gonna beat
the shit outta you!

